solution.p:
From the reduced row echelon form, we see that the homogeneous equation leads to the equations
\begin{alignedat}{5} x_1 \amp \amp \amp \amp \amp {}+{} \amp 2x_4 \amp {}={} \amp 0 \\ \amp \amp x_2 \amp {}-{} \amp 2x_3 \amp {}+{} \amp x_4 \amp {}={} \amp 0\text{,} \\ \end{alignedat}
which leads to the parametric description
\xvec=\fourvec{x_1}{x_2}{x_3}{x_4} = \fourvec{-2x_4}{2x_3-x_4}{x_3}{x_4} = x_3\fourvec{0}{2}{1}{0} + x_4\fourvec{2}{-1}{0}{1}\text{.}
